Edou the chaotic monk was in luck; the (rustic) minetown temple was
dedicated to Huan Ti. Cash was respectible, but too short to buy a *lot*
of protection; the first purchase only knocked off two points of AC. And
thanks to a poly trap there was a stone golem below cutting off a good
source of funds, but Edou had an idea.

Sacrificing had brought Stormbringer, so just tossing it up in the air
cold drain enough levels to buy three or four times as much protection as
she could have gotten otherwise. Those levels could easily have been
gotten back from the cave spiders and orcs that had been put to sleep
before she entered the temple.

So on went a hard helmet and up went Stormy. Down to level 3, still have
21hp, so worth one more try. Ouch! Now only 7 hp at level 2. But now AC
will be cheap. Edou got down to a naked AC of 1, walked out of the temple
at -8, and down the dark corridor into a pair of rothes and a gray
unicorn. Oh yeah, no more warning.... DYWYPI?

